"If $t \\le 60$, then the amusement park makes a profit of $70t$ dollars. If $t > 60$, then the amusement park makes a profit of $6000 - (t - 60)$ dollars. We want to find the largest $t$ such that the profit is greater than $4200$.\n\nIf $t \\le 60$, then $70t > 4200$, which gives $t > 60$. Therefore, the largest $t$ in this case is $61$.\n\nIf $t > 60$, then $6000 - (t - 60) > 4200$, which gives $t < 1860$. Therefore, the largest $t$ in this case is $1859$.\n\nTherefore, the largest $t$ which will bring the amusement park a profit greater than $\\$4200$ is the smaller of $61$ and $1859$, which is $\\boxed{1859}$.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $1859$. I hope it is correct."
