"To simplify the expression \\(\\frac{2s^5}{s^3} - 6s^2 + \\frac{7s^3}{s}\\), we will simplify each term individually and then combine like terms.\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{2s^5}{s^3}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2s^5}{s^3} = 2s^{5-3} = 2s^2\n   \\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{7s^3}{s}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7s^3}{s} = 7s^{3-1} = 7s^2\n   \\]\n\nNow, substitute these simplified terms back into the original expression:\n\\[\n2s^2 - 6s^2 + 7s^2\n\\]\n\nCombine the like terms:\n\\[\n(2 - 6 + 7)s^2 = 3s^2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3s^2}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(3s^2\\)."
