"To find \\( f(3) \\), we need to use the given functions \\( f(x) = g(g(x)) - g(x) \\) and \\( g(x) = 2x - 1 \\).\n\nFirst, let's find \\( g(3) \\):\n\\[ g(3) = 2(3) - 1 = 6 - 1 = 5 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\( g(g(3)) \\):\n\\[ g(g(3)) = g(5) \\]\n\nNow, let's find \\( g(5) \\):\n\\[ g(5) = 2(5) - 1 = 10 - 1 = 9 \\]\n\nNow, we can find \\( f(3) \\):\n\\[ f(3) = g(g(3)) - g(3) \\]\n\\[ f(3) = g(5) - g(3) \\]\n\\[ f(3) = 9 - 5 \\]\n\\[ f(3) = 4 \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[ f(3) = \\boxed{4} \\]"
