"To compute the square of 989 without a calculator, we can use the formula for the square of a binomial:\n\n\\[\n(a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\n\\]\n\nHere, we can express 989 as \\(1000 - 1\\). So, \\(a = 1000\\) and \\(b = -1\\).\n\nApplying the formula:\n\n\\[\n(1000 - 1)^2 = 1000^2 + 2 \\cdot 1000 \\cdot (-1) + (-1)^2\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n1000^2 = 100000\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 1000 \\cdot (-1) = -2000\n\\]\n\\[\n(-1)^2 = 1\n\\]\n\nAdd these results together:\n\n\\[\n100000 - 2000 + 1 = 98001\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{98001}\\)."
