"Let \\( c \\) be the number of clowns and \\( h \\) be the number of horses. We know two things:\n1. Each clown has 2 legs and 1 head.\n2. Each horse has 4 legs and 1 head.\n\nFrom the given information, we can set up the following equations:\n1. The total number of legs: \\( 2c + 4h = 30 \\)\n2. The total number of heads: \\( c + h = 10 \\)\n\nWe can solve these equations simultaneously. First, let's simplify the first equation by dividing everything by 2:\n\\[ c + 2h = 15 \\]\n\nNow we have the system of equations:\n\\[ c + h = 10 \\]\n\\[ c + 2h = 15 \\]\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[ (c + 2h) - (c + h) = 15 - 10 \\]\n\\[ h = 5 \\]\n\nSo, the number of horses is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $5$. I hope it is correct."
