"To solve the equation \\( |x + 3| = 6 \\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The equation \\( |x + 3| = 6 \\) can be split into two separate equations:\n\n1. \\( x + 3 = 6 \\)\n2. \\( x + 3 = -6 \\)\n\nLet's solve each equation separately:\n\n1. \\( x + 3 = 6 \\)\n   Subtract 3 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   x = 6 - 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. \\( x + 3 = -6 \\)\n   Subtract 3 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   x = -6 - 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = -9\n   \\]\n\nThe solutions to the equation are \\( x = 3 \\) and \\( x = -9 \\). The positive difference between these solutions is:\n\\[\n|3 - (-9)| = |3 + 9| = 12\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\)."
"To find the expression for \\( f(2x) \\), we start by substituting \\( 2x \\) into the function \\( f(x) = x^2 - 3x + 4 \\).\n\n\\[\nf(2x) = (2x)^2 - 3(2x) + 4\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify each term:\n\n\\[\n(2x)^2 = 4x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n-3(2x) = -6x\n\\]\n\\[\n4 = 4\n\\]\n\nPutting it all together, we get:\n\n\\[\nf(2x) = 4x^2 - 6x + 4\n\\]\n\nThus, the expression for \\( f(2x) \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4x^2 - 6x + 4}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\( 4x^2 - 6x + 4 \\). I hope it is correct."
