"First, we complete the square for both $x$ and $y$ terms.\n\nFor the $x$ terms:\n$$x^2 + 6x = (x + 3)^2 - 9$$\n\nFor the $y$ terms:\n$$y^2 - 12y = (y - 6)^2 - 36$$\n\nSubstitute these back into the original equation:\n$$(x + 3)^2 - 9 + (y - 6)^2 - 36 - 4 = 0$$\n\nSimplify:\n$$(x + 3)^2 + (y - 6)^2 - 49 = 0$$\n\nThis is the equation of a circle with center $(-3, 6)$ and radius $\\sqrt{49} = 7$.\n\nThe circumference $C$ of a circle is given by:\n$$C = 2\\pi r$$\n\nSubstitute the radius $r = 7$:\n$$C = 2\\pi \\cdot 7 = 14\\pi$$\n\nTherefore, the circumference of the circle is:\n$$C = \\boxed{14\\pi}$$"
