"To find \\(\\angle OBC\\) in acute triangle \\(ABC\\) where \\(\\angle A = 68^\\circ\\) and \\(O\\) is the circumcenter, we can use the properties of the circumcenter and the angles in the triangle.\n\nFirst, recall that the circumcenter \\(O\\) of a triangle is the point where the perpendicular bisectors of the sides intersect. The angle \\(\\angle OBC\\) is an inscribed angle that subtends the arc \\(BC\\).\n\nIn an acute triangle, the measure of an inscribed angle is half the measure of the central angle that subtends the same arc. Therefore, \\(\\angle OBC\\) is half of \\(\\angle BAC\\).\n\nGiven \\(\\angle BAC = 68^\\circ\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\angle OBC = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 68^\\circ = 34^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the measure of \\(\\angle OBC\\) is \\(\\boxed{34^\\circ}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(34^\\circ\\). I hope it is correct."
