"Since $CX$ bisects $\\angle ACB$, we have $\\angle ACX = \\angle BCX = \\frac{1}{2} \\angle ACB = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 90^\\circ = 45^\\circ$.\n\nNow, we can use the Law of Cosines in $\\triangle ACX$ to find $AX$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\nAX^2 &= AC^2 + CX^2 - 2 \\cdot AC \\cdot CX \\cdot \\cos(\\angle ACX) \\\\\n&= 21^2 + 45^2 - 2 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 45 \\cdot \\cos(45^\\circ) \\\\\n&= 441 + 2025 - 2 \\cdot 21 \\cdot 45 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= 441 + 2025 - 2025 \\\\\n&= 441\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, $AX = \\sqrt{441} = \\boxed{21}$.\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $21$. I hope it is correct."
