"To find the distance between two points on the complex plane, we use the distance formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\(x_1 = 1\\), \\(y_1 = -4\\), \\(x_2 = -4\\), and \\(y_2 = 2\\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{((-4) - 1)^2 + (2 - (-4))^2}\n\\]\n\nSimplify inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{(-5)^2 + 6^2}\n\\]\n\nCalculate the squares:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{25 + 36}\n\\]\n\nAdd the results:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\sqrt{61}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between Matt's and Marie's points is \\(\\sqrt{61}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(\\sqrt{61}\\)."
