"To find the number of positive even perfect cubes less than 2008, we need to determine the largest integer \\( n \\) such that \\( n^3 < 2008 \\).\n\nFirst, we find the cube root of 2008:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{2008} \\approx 12.64\n\\]\n\nThe largest integer less than 12.64 is 12. Therefore, we need to check the cubes of even integers from 2 to 12.\n\nThe even integers from 2 to 12 are: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, and 12.\n\nWe calculate their cubes:\n\\[\n2^3 = 8, \\quad 4^3 = 64, \\quad 6^3 = 216, \\quad 8^3 = 512, \\quad 10^3 = 1000, \\quad 12^3 = 1728\n\\]\n\nThere are \\(\\boxed{6}\\) positive even perfect cubes less than 2008."
