"Let's denote the original number by \\( x \\).\n\nAccording to the problem, if the original number is multiplied by five, the result is the same as twenty-one plus twice the original number. We can express this relationship mathematically as:\n\n\\[ 5x = 21 + 2x \\]\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation for \\( x \\).\n\nFirst, let's isolate the terms involving \\( x \\) on one side of the equation. We can do this by subtracting \\( 2x \\) from both sides:\n\n\\[ 5x - 2x = 21 \\]\n\nSimplifying the left side, we get:\n\n\\[ 3x = 21 \\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\( x \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 3:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{21}{3} \\]\n\nSimplifying the right side, we get:\n\n\\[ x = 7 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the original number is \\( \\boxed{7} \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\( 7 \\). I hope it is correct."
