"To compute \\((-49) \\div 7\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the signs of the numbers involved.\n2. Divide the absolute values of the numbers.\n3. Apply the appropriate sign to the result.\n\nStep 1: Identify the signs of the numbers.\n- The number \\(-49\\) is negative.\n- The number \\(7\\) is positive.\n\nStep 2: Divide the absolute values of the numbers.\n- The absolute value of \\(-49\\) is \\(49\\).\n- The absolute value of \\(7\\) is \\(7\\).\n- Divide \\(49\\) by \\(7\\):\n  \\[\n  49 \\div 7 = 7\n  \\]\n\nStep 3: Apply the appropriate sign to the result.\n- Since \\(-49\\) is negative and \\(7\\) is positive, the result of the division will be negative.\n- Therefore, the result is \\(-7\\).\n\nThus, \\((-49) \\div 7 = -7\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(-7\\). I hope it is correct."
"First, let's determine the positions of the hour and minute hands at 2:48 PM.\n\n- At 2:00 PM, the hour hand is at the 2.\n- At 2:48 PM, the hour hand has moved \\(\\frac{48}{60} \\times 30 = 24\\) degrees past the 2.\n- Therefore, the hour hand is at \\(2 + 24 = 26\\) degrees.\n\n- At 2:00 PM, the minute hand is at the 12.\n- At 2:48 PM, the minute hand is at the 48, which is \\(48 \\times 6 = 288\\) degrees from the 12.\n\nThe angle between the hour and minute hands is the absolute difference between their positions:\n\\[ |288 - 26| = 262 \\text{ degrees} \\]\n\nSince the smaller obtuse angle formed by the hands of a clock is the smaller of the two angles, it is 262 degrees.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{262}\\)."
