"First, let's simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2^{20} + 2^{20} + 2^{20} + 2^{21}\n\\]\n\nNotice that there are three terms of \\(2^{20}\\) and one term of \\(2^{21}\\). We can factor out \\(2^{20}\\) from the first three terms:\n\n\\[\n2^{20} (1 + 1 + 1) + 2^{21} = 2^{20} \\cdot 3 + 2^{21} = 3 \\cdot 2^{20} + 2^{21}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to divide this expression by \\(2^{17}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 \\cdot 2^{20} + 2^{21}}{2^{17}} = 3 \\cdot 2^{20-17} + 2^{21-17} = 3 \\cdot 1 + 4 = 7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7}\n\\]"
