"To find the perimeter of the regular hexagon, we first need to determine the side length of one equilateral triangle. Given that the perimeter of one equilateral triangle is 39 inches, we can find the side length by dividing the perimeter by the number of sides.\n\nAn equilateral triangle has three sides, so the side length \\( s \\) of one equilateral triangle is:\n\\[\ns = \\frac{39}{3} = 13 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nSince the regular hexagon is divided into six congruent equilateral triangles, each side of the hexagon is the same as the side length of one equilateral triangle. Therefore, the side length of the hexagon is also 13 inches.\n\nA regular hexagon has six sides, so the perimeter \\( P \\) of the hexagon is:\n\\[\nP = 6 \\times \\text{side length} = 6 \\times 13 = 78 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of the regular hexagon is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{78}\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is 78 inches. I hope it is correct."
