"To determine the minimum number of weeks it takes for every pair of people to hug at least once, we need to consider the structure of the problem and the nature of the hugs.\n\nEach person in the pew hugs exactly two people per week (one to their left and one to their right). Since there are 8 people in the pew, the total number of hugs per week is:\n\n\\[ 8 \\times 2 = 16 \\]\n\nEach hug involves two people, so the total number of unique pairs of people is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{2} \\), where \\( n \\) is the number of people. For 8 people:\n\n\\[ \\binom{8}{2} = \\frac{8 \\times 7}{2 \\times 1} = 28 \\]\n\nThis means there are 28 unique pairs of people. Since each pair of people hugs at most once per week, the minimum number of weeks required for every pair of people to hug at least once is simply the number of unique pairs, which is 28.\n\nTherefore, the minimum number of weeks required is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{28} \\]"
