"To compute the matrix-vector product \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we perform the following multiplications:\n\n1. Multiply the first row of the matrix by the vector:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} = 1 \\cdot 5 + 2 \\cdot 3 = 5 + 6 = 11\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply the second row of the matrix by the vector:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 8 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} = 4 \\cdot 5 + 8 \\cdot 3 = 20 + 24 = 44\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the result of the matrix-vector product is:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\\\ 44 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\\\ 44 \\end{pmatrix}}\\)."
