"We can combine the fractions by finding a common denominator:\n\n\\[\\frac{\\cos x}{1 - \\sin x} - \\frac{\\cos x}{1 + \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x(1 + \\sin x) - \\cos x(1 - \\sin x)}{(1 - \\sin x)(1 + \\sin x)}.\\]\n\nSimplifying the numerator, we get:\n\n\\[\\cos x(1 + \\sin x) - \\cos x(1 - \\sin x) = \\cos x + \\cos x \\sin x - \\cos x + \\cos x \\sin x = 2 \\cos x \\sin x.\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\\frac{2 \\cos x \\sin x}{(1 - \\sin x)(1 + \\sin x)} = \\frac{2 \\cos x \\sin x}{1 - \\sin^2 x}.\\]\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity \\(\\cos^2 x + \\sin^2 x = 1\\), we have:\n\n\\[\\frac{2 \\cos x \\sin x}{1 - \\sin^2 x} = \\boxed{\\cos x \\sin x}.\\]"
